## Installation
Inside the repository, `pnpm install` links the local packages. Outside the repository, install the tarball (`pnpm pack:all` → `dist/npm`).

```sh
npm install ./agent-console-<name>-{{version}}.tgz
```

## Minimal usage
```ts readme
import { describePackage } from "{{name}}";

const info = describePackage();
```

`info` is `"{{name}}@{{version}}"`. This block must match `test/readme.test.ts`.

## Development and standalone reuse
- `pnpm build`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, and `pnpm test` each run on their own inside this folder.
- The public API is only the paths listed in `exports`. Other packages do not import `src/` or `dist/` directly.
- Check that the package still works when copied out of the repository with `pnpm portability --package {{name}}`.
